<title>FRANCE: French police to curb attacks on Spanish truckers.</title>
<headline>French police to curb attacks on Spanish truckers.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>French police and justice authorities have been ordered to crack down on French farmers attacking Spanish truckers transporting fruit and vegetables in southern France, French officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Spain lashed out at Paris on Wednesday for what it called the passivity of authorities in the face of the repeated attacks. Despite a French apology, Madrid has also complained to the European Union, asking for measures to be taken against Paris.</p>
<p>Over the past week, French farmers who want tighter controls on imported produce have stopped Spanish trucks to dump and burn their fresh fruits and vegetables.</p>
<p>A Spanish truck driver was in hospital in Montpellier, France after being attacked earlier this week.</p>
</text>
